The LUKS header is the part of the partition that holds all the keys and the
corresponding key slots. This is a tiny portion of the partition that, if
corrupted, will render the entire filesystem unusable and all data on it lost.
For this reason, it is advisable to create a backup of the header and put it in
a safe location. Should the original header get corrupted, you can restore this
header with the command
"cryptsetup luksHeaderRestore  --header-backup-file=<header-backup> <LUKS-partition>"
Creating a backup of the LUKS header has no impact on its locked state. After
restoring it, you will still need access to your enrolled secrets to unlock the
encrypted partition.
